    <!-- ── v2.1.1 ───────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <item>
      <title>MachStruct 2.1.1</title>
      <description><![CDATA[
        <h3>Fixed</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><b>Object keys appeared in the wrong order, and repeated keys
              vanished</b>, in files under 5 MB. Saving wrote back the
              truncated version. Structure now comes from the file&rsquo;s
              bytes at every size, so a document reads the same whatever its
              size &mdash; and small files parse slightly faster.</li>
          <li><b>Opening two documents at once could show one file&rsquo;s data
              in the other, or hang the app.</b> Search results, breadcrumbs
              and X-Ray schemas could report another document&rsquo;s contents,
              and navigating to a search result could consume gigabytes of
              memory until the app was force-quit.</li>
          <li><b>Whole-number decimals such as <code>1.0</code> were displayed
              and re-saved as <code>1</code></b>, losing the number type and
              silently rewriting the file.</li>
          <li><b>The download link on machstruct.com returned a 404 for some
              releases.</b> Every release now publishes a versionless disk
              image.</li>
        </ul>
      ]]></description>
      <pubDate>Mon, 19 Oct 2026 15:30:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <sparkle:version>6</sparkle:version>
